Derived Microban hardware parts
Copyright (c) 2026 Marc Duclusaud (original parts), modifications 2026 Masaaki Hijikata

All files here are made by tools/make_parts.py from Microban's cad/step files
(https://github.com/Rhoban/microban, commit d0a128d180ecfce69eaaf31b295a0fce31280bfd):

- foot_sole80.stl/.step: foot.step with 10 mm cut off the toe end of the sole
  plate, so that the ground-contact plate is 80 mm long (ROBO-ONE Light: at most
  55 % of the leg length). Nothing else is changed.
- ankle_block_integrated_{right,left}.stl/.step: ankle_dbl_block.step with a
  printed hinge body (stub axles on the ankle-pitch axis, shank-bar pivot boss)
  fused into it in place of the ankle-pitch servo.
- hip_block_integrated_{right,left}.stl/.step: hip_dbl_block_{right,left}.step
  with the thigh bar's upper pivot support grown out of it.
- head_integrated.stl/.step: head.step with the old servo-horn seat on its
  underside filled and a hollow neck stalk grown out of it in place of the
  neck servo.

